        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Manzikert</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">26 August 1071</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Near Manzikert, in the theme of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malazgirt">Malazgirt</a> in Muş Province, eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> under the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanos-iv-diogenes">Romanos IV Diogenes</a>, with a host of around 40,000 men before it was divided; the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire</a> under the sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alp-arslan">Alp Arslan</a>, with allies and 30,000 cavalry from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aleppo">Aleppo</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosul">Mosul</a>, joined by a force of Kurdish fighters estimated at 10,000 sent by the Marwanid emir</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Byzantine army was routed and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romanos-iv-diogenes">Romanos</a> IV was wounded and taken prisoner. After a week he was released on agreed terms, but he was soon deposed and blinded in a civil war.</span></div>
